  "text": "Claymoon by Adam Weismann, is a series of hand-formed clay artworks by Adam Weismann that speak of the rhythms of nature, the beauty of imperfection and the processes of deep time. Claymoon holds a particular fascination with the aesthetic and functional properties of clay, and one that began when Adam Weismann, along with his wife Katy Bryce, founded Clayworks in 2010. Clayworks came from a shared love of nature and a belief in natural and sustainable building practices. Weismann and Bryce travelled the world to learn about vernacular traditions of building with clay and whilst initially focused on the integrity and performance of the material, they also saw the capacity of natural materials to affect the way we experience the spaces we inhabit. This fascination has continued into the work of Claymoon, which also passively effect the environment in the space in which they are shown. For further information on pricing and availability for Adam’s work, please contact info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk Artworks Clay 1666, 2025 Back to Artists Bespoke Commissions Golden Earth Studio offers a bespoke commission service that utilises the construction byproducts of our clients’ homes. To explore the possibilities of commissioning a unique piece of artwork to compliments your interior space, get in touch via our contact form or email. info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk First & Last Name Email Phone Message Send",
